  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Within  the interval $[0,\\pi ]$, determine the average value of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\pi ))-(-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)-(-2\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(\\frac{5}{2})-(-\\frac{3}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
